   "user": "O_oNevermore",
   "message": "off topic but another interesting thing is that subtext and dramatic tension are linked\n\nif you break the subtext by being too obvious you break the tension\n\nisn't that absolutely fascinating? why would subtext be linked to anything much less dramatic tension?\n\npartly probably because we evolved to be social guessing machines, it's the game of our species to sus out intentions and hide them\n\nbut I'd wager the broader mechanism at play is that we are learning systems, and the information gap between the subtext and the stated text introduces uncertainty which engages our dopamine/learning systems. it pushes us closer to criticality (to use the lingo from the entropic brain hypothesis).\n\ncreating spaces of information gaps are perhaps spaces of co-creation\n\nspaces of active participation with the content\n\nhttps://share.google/aimode/TyCXwRR9gVSjV5AL0",
