   "user": "Benjamin Isaac",
   "message": "unformed thoughts re: cosmos grants due 7/26 from https://www.cosmos-institute.org/grants: \nai as an educational suture\n\nscience modeling\n\nA/B/U\n\nallowing students to identify A/B/U premises in paragraphs\n\nidentify on an individual level how they follow the material. Teach them to think in terms of premises - deductive reasoning - and understand how people make deductions. \n\npilot study\n\n\nalternate: putting equations into colors. giving background on equations. translate quantitative into qualitative. this could atrophy some high level mathematics skills but I believe this would be offset by opening up the meaning in the mathematics to 80% of readers.\n\n\n\nUse A/B/U and automatically trace lines of inquiry/knowledge to calibrate\n\nAs a human, I don't know which will be easy and which will be hard. AI was expected to be solved in x months, after all. \n\nI know I love learning, that I have stopped when the equations got to hard, and that explainers visually, etc, form a valuable bridge to mathematics knowlege and understanding, e.g. 3b1b. if you're just trying to do chemistry, doing calculus by hand isn't necessary any more. But understanding that's going on is important in terms of energy. Builds links between concepts. AI's are good at these.\n\n\nhelp with the 'i don't remember what it feels like not to know this' problem, and the 'i'm embarrassed to ask questions' problem. The second, if trained via ai, teaches valuable skills. And it can help by giving a metric - understanding of the material at a certain level - for asking a person for help too.\n\nLOCAL IS KEY\n\nlaptop based\ngpt4all\nspeed limits use without thinking\n\n\nI study myself not knowing things.\n\nHow it feels in your body - what language works. \n\n\nori - sponeous associations rallying together around common interests.\n\ni used ai for the transcript here. \n\n\"spontaneous Association of individuals who from the bottom up 6 were rallying together around common interests ' from 6:30 of cosmos intro video",
